{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqd3aFoE5b5kD2Dd4Zg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new UI's sessions aren't recorded because `NewApp` never wraps its `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`. The legacy shell does wrap it, which is why its replays work. I wrapped `NewApp` the same way and added a comment in both shells. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n**Why:** Replay on mobile is made from screenshots, and the SDK takes them inside `PostHogWidget` (`posthog_flutter` 5.55.0, `lib/src/posthog_widget.dart`). Without it, events, screen tracking and taps still arrive, which is why Events looks healthy. There are simply no frames to record. Nothing in the PostHog project settings is involved, since both groups share the same config and SDK version.\n\n**Fix:** `lib/new_app.dart` now returns `PostHogWidget(child: MaterialApp.router(...))`. `lib/legacy_app.dart` only got the explanatory comment.\n\n**Verification:** `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I have not run the app on a device or checked a session in PostHog, so the replay fix is unconfirmed until that happens. Steps are in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was deployed or submitted.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- `ANSWER.md` at the repo root has the full write-up.\n- Running `flutter analyze` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml` and generated `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/`. I reverted and removed those, so the diff only touches the two shell files and `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":36866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30df3bad-7956-47d1-9e69-